  "title": "Emotion Supercharges Memory",
  "emoji": "🗃️",
  "color": "#6D28D9",
  "description": "A tiny lesson with a big payoff: Emotion Supercharges Memory.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "You remember exactly where you were during a shocking news event but not what you ate last Tuesday.",
      "visual": "📺"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Emotional experiences trigger the amygdala, which signals the hippocampus to pay extra attention.",
      "visual": "🚨"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "Stress hormones like adrenaline and cortisol enhance encoding of emotionally charged events.",
      "visual": "💉"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "But too much stress reverses the effect—chronic anxiety actually impairs memory formation.",
      "visual": "😰"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Flashbulb memories feel vivid and accurate, yet studies show they're often distorted over time.",
      "visual": "📸"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Emotion makes memories stick—but not necessarily makes them true.",
      "visual": "🎭"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "How does chronic stress affect memory?",
    "options": [
      "It impairs memory formation",
      "It dramatically improves it",
      "It has no measurable effect"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
